  "reconstructibility": 2,
  "reason": "R8 and R18 provide a close analogue: adding Cr to a BCC refractory alloy containing W/V/Ta/Ti produces a network-distributed Cr2Ta Laves phase and raises hardness through combined solid-solution and Laves-phase precipitation strengthening. R6 independently establishes Laves-phase formation within a Cr-containing refractory BCC matrix, while R1 and related records show that minor alloying can sometimes improve strength without sacrificing, and even while increasing, plasticity. Thus an expert could plausibly transfer Cr addition to HfMoTaTiZr and investigate an interconnected multicomponent Cr-rich Laves phase as a strengthening and crack-deflecting mediator. The exact 4.2 at.% dosage and the specific plasticity-compensation role of the reticulated phase are not directly disclosed, but the intervention and principal structural-strengthening mechanism are strongly suggested."
